{"id": "EUVD-2026-93282", "enisaUuid": "89ab6623-03dd-3cc7-b196-f219fedde979", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_core: Fix queuing tx_work after workqueue is drained\n\nhci_send_acl(), hci_send_sco() and hci_send_iso() queue hdev->tx_work\nunconditionally. They can run from the L2CAP/SCO/ISO socket send path\nwhile hci_dev_close_sync() is draining hdev->workqueue (HCIDEVDOWN\nracing with a socket write). Since that queue_work() is not chained\nwork from the tx_work worker itself, __queue_work() sees the queue\nmarked __WQ_DRAINING, warns \"cannot queue %ps on wq %s\", and drops\nthe work:\n\n  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 5985 at kernel/workqueue.c:2352 __queue_work\n  Call Trace:\n   queue_work_on\n   l2cap_chan_send\n   l2cap_sock_sendmsg\n   ...\n\nhci_dev_close_sync() already sets HCI_CMD_DRAIN_WORKQUEUE before\ndraining, but only hci_cmd_work() and handle_cmd_cnt_and_timer()\ncheck it before queuing. Route the tx_work producers through the\nsame guard via a shared hci_sched_tx() helper.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8010212197d4a3ee714f78ed77048d0b712ff925", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab0678a0701ac4de499428dc1b321659bb74d272", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e220c1242a643d97102a79f09b7ef3aa31276961", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbb325bc150e8c0dbce004ac0e5516bcffc0de31", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6610c6fe4b8936c232048e6049bf77c70a6f759c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98297", "GHSA-mvfp-xjr6-rmvq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ded68d7-9b03-32b6-9fec-e8a672815a29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "12579275-341c-36f6-86a2-38bae408872b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "2f5a97f7-1409-304b-9354-f9babfa933af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "2faf2bcc-4a31-3935-9778-dca49a5f6175", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "60bceb9a4c693e68cc90ba4b2dfb9e000e8638ff"}, {"id": "5318d604-daaa-329e-b09d-91a07a290b24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "525daaea459fc215f432de1b8debbd9144bf97b0 <cbb325bc150e8c0dbce004ac0e5516bcffc0de31"}, {"id": "56e42a68-98d1-358e-8463-9255fb99d52a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9cebe4680bb9a72f80c6541eb24af06db7a1fbc9 <ab0678a0701ac4de499428dc1b321659bb74d272"}, {"id": "56f781b7-106b-3a61-aae6-56f298130361", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7b81c1378b79c3143ca3fdb3d18ac0f01cbabb21 <8010212197d4a3ee714f78ed77048d0b712ff925"}, {"id": "76693954-0407-30e3-bc0e-4b9ebc0525a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8105bff6-e2bc-3534-a36e-a8d0d1497b4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.35 <6.18.54"}, {"id": "82668e04-8f95-31f2-b2fd-3df9fa44cf53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47330cc875b36a1cf7b3543cb2cf90a7c603ce0e <e220c1242a643d97102a79f09b7ef3aa31276961"}, {"id": "8746c924-ad7f-3309-9a24-67fe0134e7f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0.12 <7.1"}, {"id": "9974538c-de66-3c4c-80ae-e9caa93386e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c35b3e50-954f-3f88-a646-24653093bb09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "525daaea459fc215f432de1b8debbd9144bf97b0 <6610c6fe4b8936c232048e6049bf77c70a6f759c"}, {"id": "d15c4bac-cff2-342e-8fca-a9758579089c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_v